  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 334 AM EDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nNext week will remain dry with temperatures generally on a warming \ntrend, especially by late week. Surface high pressure will remain \nthe dominant feature, keeping things dry through the end of the \nmonth. Meanwhile, a persistent ridge aloft will flatten to some \ndegree midweek as a trough sweeps from the Plains into the Upper \nMississippi Valley, though the ridge looks to build back over the \nSoutheast by late week. \n\nAll of this is to say that mostly sunny and dry conditions will \nremain the dominant theme through the end of the month. High \ntemperatures will largely remain in the 70s and lows in the 40s to \nlow 50s. Any chance for rainfall will hold off until early November \nwhen flow looks to become more southwesterly ahead of a potentially \nmore active pattern, though this remains beyond the end of the \ncurrent forecast period and details remain highly nebulous.",
